708
01:05:15,744 --> 01:05:20,629
Let's.... Let's keep the wife at a
distance for now, as well.

709
01:05:21,578 --> 01:05:23,217
I'd like to see him.

710
01:05:23,697 --> 01:05:27,257
Can you arrange that?
Look, I won't lie to you.

711
01:05:27,573 --> 01:05:31,169
Alex was so nervous, we had to sedate him.

712
01:05:31,169 --> 01:05:33,927
I looked in his eyes and
I couldn't see my husband.

713
01:05:33,927 --> 01:05:38,095
And then he just shoots a man in front
of our son. That's not sedation.

714
01:05:39,043 --> 01:05:42,403
He's responding to drugs differently now.

715
01:05:44,199 --> 01:05:46,763
We both knew from day one,

716
01:05:47,196 --> 01:05:49,920
there would be complications.

717
01:05:53,990 --> 01:05:56,236
Just give me a little more time.

718
01:05:56,987 --> 01:05:58,790
I promise,

719
01:05:59,705 --> 01:06:01,905
you will have your husband back.

720
01:06:03,941 --> 01:06:07,897
This goes for every squad
in every department.

721
01:06:07,897 --> 01:06:14,211
Detective Murphy will have full access to all
investigations. Robberies, narcotics, homicides.

722
01:06:14,211 --> 01:06:18,487
If he requests to take over a case,
the case will be handed to him.

723
01:06:18,487 --> 01:06:21,605
No arguments, no complaints.
This is bullshit.

724
01:06:21,605 --> 01:06:25,602
I said no complaints.
And I mean it. Now...

725
01:06:26,202 --> 01:06:29,238
Good morning, Chief Dean.
Good morning, officers.

726
01:06:29,238 --> 01:06:32,599
I have selected 13 targets for
today, all wanted for murder.

727
01:06:32,599 --> 01:06:36,072
John Biggs is target number one.
I will be taking over this case.

728
01:06:36,072 --> 01:06:40,668
Ambulances, detention vehicles, and coroners
should be ready to move in on my request.

729
01:06:40,668 --> 01:06:42,915
I wish you all a very good day.

730
01:06:50,061 --> 01:06:51,466
Murphy.

731
01:06:51,939 --> 01:06:53,549
You okay, man?

732
01:06:55,216 --> 01:06:57,099
I am fine, Sergeant.

733
01:06:57,414 --> 01:06:59,372
Can't wait to get back to work.

734
01:06:59,372 --> 01:07:03,133
Lake and Daniels are in there shitting their
pants... Excuse me, I have casework.

735
01:07:54,564 --> 01:07:57,560
Don't shoot. Don't shoot.
Don't shoot. Don't shoot.

736
01:08:03,756 --> 01:08:07,352
Walter Karrel, look at me.
You have two options.

737
01:08:07,352 --> 01:08:08,553
Option one.

738
01:08:09,391 --> 01:08:14,765
I shoot you with 50,000 volts which may
cause respiratory failure, organ malfunction,

739
01:08:14,765 --> 01:08:19,221
internal burns, and loss of bowel and
bladder control. And then I arrest you.

740
01:08:19,221 --> 01:08:23,258
Option two. You tell me where
John Biggs' drug lab is located.

741
01:08:23,258 --> 01:08:25,539
And then I arrest you.

742
01:08:26,096 --> 01:08:28,615
You have two seconds to decide.

743
01:09:37,114 --> 01:09:40,950
Totally justifiable.
We are going to make a lot of money.

744
01:09:40,950 --> 01:09:44,786
Nothing. No fear.
No increase in heart rate.

745
01:09:44,786 --> 01:09:48,306
No traces of anger whatsoever.

746
01:09:48,306 --> 01:09:50,903
Congratulations, Doctor.

747
01:09:50,903 --> 01:09:52,585
You did it.

748
01:09:53,619 --> 01:09:55,308
Yes, I did.

749
01:10:03,451 --> 01:10:07,886
I told you, sir. Norton clearly
never had control of the product.

750
01:10:07,886 --> 01:10:11,008
I agree.
And that's why I called you here.

751
01:10:11,008 --> 01:10:15,120
I just want a second pair of eyes
on this thing, that's all. Okay.

752
01:10:15,120 --> 01:10:19,356
I will need a feed from the Tin Man's head
plus full surveillance of the lab, and...

753
01:10:19,356 --> 01:10:21,954
You're going to have full
access to everything.

754
01:10:21,954 --> 01:10:25,800
If anything comes up,
I am going to be in Washington.

755
01:10:29,628 --> 01:10:33,744
He brought peace to this country's
most violent city.

756
01:10:33,744 --> 01:10:38,144
He showed us all that Detroit and
America can have a brighter future.

757
01:10:38,580 --> 01:10:42,145
A future of economic growth,
freedom, and happiness.

758
01:10:42,145 --> 01:10:50,129
On tonight's show, a visionary and true
patriot. The CEO of Omnicorp, Raymond Sellars.

759
01:10:52,448 --> 01:10:54,725
- Hello, Pat.
- Raymond. Thanks for having me.

760
01:10:54,725 --> 01:10:58,362
You must be doing a
victory lap about now. Well.

761
01:10:58,362 --> 01:11:02,398
Two weeks ago, Omni's stock
went through the roof.

762
01:11:02,398 --> 01:11:06,914
And the Senate has finally agreed
to vote on the repeal of the Dreyfus Act.

763
01:11:06,914 --> 01:11:10,471
Well, look, I mean, the
tide is definitely turning. I...

764
01:11:10,471 --> 01:11:13,388
I just feel certain that soon we will
be keeping all Americans safe.

765
01:11:13,388 --> 01:11:14,589
I certainly hope so.

766
01:11:14,589 --> 01:11:18,985
But, I think our next guest will have
a different point of view. Mmm-hmm.

767
01:11:18,985 --> 01:11:20,469
Hubert Dreyfus.

768
01:11:20,783 --> 01:11:24,579
Senator, thank you for joining us.
Hello, Pat. Mr. Sellars.

769
01:11:24,579 --> 01:11:27,056
Senator, do you know what this is?

770
01:11:27,056 --> 01:11:31,452
The American public is
divided on the Dreyfus Act.

771
01:11:31,452 --> 01:11:36,780
Our polls at Novakelement.com
are tight at 50-50.

772
01:11:36,780 --> 01:11:44,201
There is no doubt Omnicorp created a sensation
but this bill is not about Alex Murphy.

773
01:11:44,201 --> 01:11:49,117
It's about whether America's willing to give
robots the authority over human lives. No. No.

774
01:11:49,117 --> 01:11:54,272
Look, look, look. This sea change
we're witnessing, and it is a sea change,

775
01:11:54,272 --> 01:11:59,468
shows that Americans don't really care if our
law enforcement systems are manned or unmanned.

776
01:11:59,468 --> 01:12:03,904
What they care about is efficiency and they
care about safety. You're clouding the issue.

777
01:12:03,904 --> 01:12:08,140
This is clearly an attempt to sway
public opinion with a marketing stunt. No.

778
01:12:08,140 --> 01:12:13,176
What's clear is that with just one system
in place, we have cut crime by 80%.

779
01:12:13,176 --> 01:12:17,700
Just imagine if we put, I don't know,
let's say 100 systems in place.

780
01:12:17,700 --> 01:12:21,409
And then, I want you to ask yourself,
why are you holding us back?

781
01:12:21,409 --> 01:12:24,966
Is that your plan? Thank you, Senator.
And thank you, Raymond. Thank you, Pat.

782
01:12:24,966 --> 01:12:28,009
Well, there you have it.

783
01:12:28,483 --> 01:12:32,648
Who could argue with that?
Which begs the question.

784
01:12:33,239 --> 01:12:37,884
Has the US Senate become pro-crime?

785
01:12:47,347 --> 01:12:50,514
Yeah, hi. No, no, 5000.

786
01:12:50,824 --> 01:12:52,353
Call me tomorrow.

787
01:12:53,541 --> 01:12:57,026
Hey, guys.
Vallon's waiting for you inside.

788
01:12:58,297 --> 01:13:01,419
What, you too busy to walk us in?
I am out here making money. Yeah.

789
01:13:01,419 --> 01:13:04,417
Where are my trip wires?
I got to do this myself?

790
01:13:04,652 --> 01:13:07,128
- What took you so long?
- What the hell is all this shit?

791
01:13:07,128 --> 01:13:10,177
I can't move any product with
this thing on the streets.

792
01:13:10,686 --> 01:13:14,482
What are you doing to protect me?
Relax. The guy's a walking zombie.

793
01:13:14,482 --> 01:13:16,120
And tell me your phones are off.

794
01:13:16,120 --> 01:13:18,478
He's not going after you.
We covered our tracks.

795
01:13:18,478 --> 01:13:22,725
He can't manufacture evidence out of
thin air. If he does, I am ready for him.

796
01:13:31,228 --> 01:13:32,508
Well?

797
01:13:36,144 --> 01:13:39,022
I have been getting calls. From whom?

798
01:13:39,461 --> 01:13:44,857
Well, Clara. You need to let her
see her husband. She has rights.

799
01:13:45,376 --> 01:13:48,383
That's not your decision.
That's Legal's call.

800
01:13:48,383 --> 01:13:53,018
Yeah, but it's only a question of time
before she turns up on television.

801
01:13:53,018 --> 01:13:54,852
Well, she can try.

802
01:13:55,327 --> 01:13:58,414
I will issue a gag order before
I let her see her husband.

803
01:13:59,643 --> 01:14:01,207
I'd hop to it.

804
01:14:01,502 --> 01:14:04,850
Alex. Alex. Alex.

805
01:14:06,797 --> 01:14:11,142
Alex. You need to come home.
Clara, please stand aside.

806
01:14:11,142 --> 01:14:14,949
You need to speak to your son.
Right now, I see three crimes in progress.

807
01:14:14,949 --> 01:14:16,559
Alex, listen to me.

808
01:14:17,827 --> 01:14:19,027
I know you're in there.

809
01:14:21,264 --> 01:14:23,703
David won't show his face at school.

810
01:14:24,421 --> 01:14:26,145
He's having nightmares.

811
01:14:27,779 --> 01:14:30,707
He's falling apart.
I am falling apart.

812
01:14:31,775 --> 01:14:33,180
Please.

813
01:14:34,812 --> 01:14:37,058
I can't do this on my own.

814
01:14:37,370 --> 01:14:40,696
He's been scared ever since that night.

815
01:14:49,959 --> 01:14:51,638
What do you think she's going to do?

816
01:14:52,277 --> 01:14:54,045
What's he going to do?

817
01:15:14,657 --> 01:15:18,382
Are you okay?
David? David.

818
01:15:18,974 --> 01:15:21,538
Stand back. Come on, stand back.

819
01:15:41,793 --> 01:15:43,991
He's supposed to be watching this.

820
01:15:43,991 --> 01:15:49,846
Instead, he's accessing images of Clara and
David arriving at school. Over and over again.

821
01:15:49,846 --> 01:15:54,906
Are you okay? Somehow, he's overriding
the system's priorities.

822
01:16:05,213 --> 01:16:09,015
- Do you want me to shut him down?
- No. Not yet.

823
01:16:10,328 --> 01:16:12,256
I want to see what happens.

824
01:16:31,949 --> 01:16:34,071
What's he doing at his house?

825
01:16:35,986 --> 01:16:39,589
Look, he's disobeying protocol.
You have to shut him down.

826
01:16:39,589 --> 01:16:42,830
As far as I can tell,
he's still doing his job.

827
01:17:42,208 --> 01:17:45,056
Adrian, give me an image of his brain.

828
01:17:46,644 --> 01:17:49,242
He's undoing what we did to him.

829
01:17:49,521 --> 01:17:55,002
His dopamine levels are coming back to normal.
How is that even possible?

830
01:17:55,996 --> 01:17:58,514
I haven't the faintest idea.

831
01:17:58,514 --> 01:18:00,203
Alex.

832
01:18:26,489 --> 01:18:29,054
Alex, please return to the station.

833
01:18:29,886 --> 01:18:31,893
I want to run some tests.

834
01:18:32,224 --> 01:18:34,372
Well, this should be interesting.

835
01:18:51,187 --> 01:18:52,465
And your phone on the table.

836
01:18:52,465 --> 01:18:54,563
We're not cops, all right?
We work for Antoine Vallon.

837
01:18:54,563 --> 01:18:57,269
- What? Whoa.
- What'd you say?

838
01:18:57,861 --> 01:18:59,902
We work for Antoine Vallon.

839
01:19:28,514 --> 01:19:30,791
My hand, man.
Where's Antoine Vallon?

840
01:19:30,791 --> 01:19:32,597
You broke my hand, man.

841
01:19:33,190 --> 01:19:35,277
I know you remember me, Jerry.

842
01:19:39,105 --> 01:19:41,302
Where's Vallon? Wait a minute.

843
01:19:41,302 --> 01:19:44,180
If I tell you where Vallon is,
he will kill my wife and kid, man.

844
01:19:45,319 --> 01:19:49,135
Your wife left you in 2019 after
filing charges for domestic abuse.

845
01:19:49,135 --> 01:19:51,223
And you don't have a kid.

846
01:19:51,494 --> 01:19:52,532
But I do.

847
01:19:54,052 --> 01:19:57,728
I am not asking again. Look, I swear, man.
I don't know where Vallon is, okay?

848
01:19:57,728 --> 01:20:01,247
The only guy I talk to is his driver Marcus.
That's it, man. That's it.

849
01:20:01,645 --> 01:20:03,732
Does he have a phone number?

850
01:20:19,869 --> 01:20:24,384
We have a problem.
Alex is breaking protocol. What's he doing?

851
01:20:24,384 --> 01:20:29,666
He's off solving his own murder.
Oh, that is genius.

852
01:20:29,666 --> 01:20:31,709
Why didn't I think of that?

853
01:20:38,533 --> 01:20:42,411
How long till he gets here?
Five minutes. All right.

854
01:20:42,411 --> 01:20:45,892
Johnny, you stay on these monitors.
What happened?

855
01:20:47,005 --> 01:20:49,888
Some idiot used an unencrypted phone.

856
01:20:51,042 --> 01:20:52,367
Shit.

857
01:21:00,394 --> 01:21:02,242
All right, everyone, listen up.

858
01:21:02,242 --> 01:21:06,912
He's coming.
He leaves alive, you don't.

859
01:21:07,867 --> 01:21:09,749
How do we stop him?

860
01:21:10,904 --> 01:21:14,264
.50 caliber and above.
Aim for the head.

861
01:21:26,051 --> 01:21:27,739
This one's set.

862
01:21:27,739 --> 01:21:30,698
Let's go. Go.
All right, move. Let's go.

863
01:21:31,886 --> 01:21:33,893
Come on. Come on.

864
01:21:35,483 --> 01:21:36,683
Ready to go.

865
01:21:37,521 --> 01:21:39,085
They're all set.

866
01:23:06,762 --> 01:23:08,247
Finish it.

867
01:23:22,429 --> 01:23:23,913
You freak, die.

868
01:24:12,944 --> 01:24:14,429
Watch out.

869
01:24:14,429 --> 01:24:18,382
Need me to call a doctor?
Come on, Jack. You're going to like this.

870
01:24:20,498 --> 01:24:23,114
What the hell you doing here?
You all going to play good cop, bad cop?

871
01:24:23,114 --> 01:24:26,344
Nah, Daniels. Bad cop, RoboCop.

872
01:24:28,091 --> 01:24:31,407
I have recovered 26 guns
from Vallon's warehouse.

873
01:24:31,407 --> 01:24:34,364
Thirteen serial numbers match
weapons missing from Evidence.

874
01:24:34,364 --> 01:24:37,522
And I got your prints all over them.
This is bullshit.

875
01:24:37,522 --> 01:24:41,558
I also have CCTV footage of you and
Vallon the same day he tried to kill me.

876
01:24:41,558 --> 01:24:43,876
So put him on the payroll.
Why we talking about this?

877
01:24:43,876 --> 01:24:47,353
It won't work. Now that his partner
got hit, he's never going to let it go.

878
01:24:47,353 --> 01:24:50,550
What is that? Lewis' hospital.
Murphy's dropping by this afternoon.

879
01:24:50,550 --> 01:24:53,588
I kill a cop, I am looking
over my shoulder...

880
01:24:53,588 --> 01:24:56,107
You know what they do
to cops in prison, man?

881
01:24:56,346 --> 01:24:59,150
Being locked up with the
same dudes you put in there?

882
01:25:02,261 --> 01:25:04,188
How long you think
before he gives you up?

883
01:25:07,736 --> 01:25:10,619
Don't shoot me. Okay?

884
01:25:11,413 --> 01:25:13,890
I swear to Christ. It was Dean.

885
01:25:13,890 --> 01:25:16,978
She helped pull those guns.
Just don't shoot me.

886
01:25:18,727 --> 01:25:20,927
Thank you for your co-operation.

887
01:25:22,843 --> 01:25:24,611
You can cuff him now, Jack.

888
01:25:33,474 --> 01:25:35,561
Now I know why we couldn't get an arrest.

889
01:25:36,671 --> 01:25:40,751
Because Vallon was protected from up on high.
Alex, I can explain.

890
01:25:41,227 --> 01:25:43,525
You tipped him off today.
Come on, man.

891
01:25:43,525 --> 01:25:49,507
Don't do this. You tried to kill me twice.
I trusted you. And you destroyed my family.

892
01:25:49,507 --> 01:25:50,819
Confess.

893
01:25:51,937 --> 01:25:54,936
Now, in front of everyone. Confess.

894
01:26:04,566 --> 01:26:08,042
What happened?
Tin Man is down. Had to be done.

895
01:26:08,042 --> 01:26:10,520
Why? Product shot a corrupt cop.

896
01:26:10,520 --> 01:26:14,757
Two more seconds, the chief's brains would
have been splattered across the 6:00 news.

897
01:26:15,037 --> 01:26:18,713
We got anything on her? Well, she's the
Chief of the Detroit Police Department.

898
01:26:18,713 --> 01:26:20,755
What do you think?

899
01:26:24,389 --> 01:26:25,918
You know what?

900
01:26:27,106 --> 01:26:30,546
This might actually tip this
thing right into the net.

901
01:26:36,778 --> 01:26:40,138
Alex, I don't know if you can hear me.

902
01:26:40,138 --> 01:26:46,289
But tonight, you uncovered a nest of vipers
inside the Detroit Police Department.

903
01:26:46,289 --> 01:26:50,810
And in so doing, you shed
light on an invaluable truth.

904
01:26:51,245 --> 01:26:57,010
Even the police, the men and women who
swore to keep us safe...

905
01:26:57,560 --> 01:26:59,283
...they can be bribed.

906
01:26:59,718 --> 01:27:02,759
They can be bought.

907
01:27:04,194 --> 01:27:08,520
Machines, however, are corruption free.

908
01:27:09,269 --> 01:27:15,106
Americans could be living in a country
where law enforcement is not only efficient,

909
01:27:15,106 --> 01:27:16,948
but incorruptible.

910
01:27:18,062 --> 01:27:22,467
Thank you, Alex, for all you have done.
And for all that you are.

911
01:27:22,738 --> 01:27:26,098
Detective Murphy is currently
in critical condition.

912
01:27:26,574 --> 01:27:29,411
Our doctors are working ceaselessly

913
01:27:29,411 --> 01:27:32,248
but, at this time, it is
unclear if he will survive.

914
01:27:32,449 --> 01:27:37,484
Ms. Kline, Ms. Kline, how do you think
the attempt on Detective Alex Murphy's life

915
01:27:37,484 --> 01:27:39,881
will affect tomorrow's
vote for the Dreyfus Act?

916
01:27:39,881 --> 01:27:44,121
At this time, Omnicorp's sole concern
is the full recovery of Detective Murphy.

917
01:27:45,038 --> 01:27:49,920
How many times does Detective Murphy
have to give his life for his country?

918
01:27:50,353 --> 01:27:55,308
I sincerely hope the Senate
makes the right vote tomorrow

919
01:27:55,308 --> 01:28:00,067
so that Alex Murphy's sacrifices
will not have been in vain.

920
01:28:04,581 --> 01:28:06,898
Senator Dreyfus is my friend.

921
01:28:06,898 --> 01:28:12,454
He has been my mentor and my strength
in times of difficulty on this floor.

922
01:28:12,734 --> 01:28:15,930
But despite all that,
I work for the state of Ohio,

923
01:28:15,930 --> 01:28:19,257
and the safety of its
citizens is my top priority.

924
01:28:19,257 --> 01:28:23,125
So I vote yes.
The Dreyfus Act must be repealed.

925
01:28:23,125 --> 01:28:28,599
That's us ahead, 39 to 10. I spoke to the
Senate liaison and it looks like it's in the bag,

926
01:28:28,599 --> 01:28:31,756
but we still have to tread
carefully with the politicians.

927
01:28:33,236 --> 01:28:35,593
We're here live at DPD headquarters

928
01:28:35,593 --> 01:28:39,709
where moments ago, Clara Murphy made
a shocking statement. What the hell?

929
01:28:39,709 --> 01:28:44,945
Omnicorp has denied me and my
son access to Alex for weeks.

930
01:28:45,425 --> 01:28:47,466
I demand to know why.

931
01:28:48,262 --> 01:28:53,464
This treatment is inhuman and somebody
needs to be held accountable.

932
01:28:54,457 --> 01:28:57,893
Oh, we're fucked.
No, we only need 12 votes.

933
01:28:57,893 --> 01:29:00,960
She shouldn't make much difference.
Yeah, but what about after the vote?

934
01:29:00,960 --> 01:29:03,768
I mean, those two should
not be allowed contact.

935
01:29:03,768 --> 01:29:09,123
If she starts putting ideas in his head...
Bring her in. I will handle the explanation.

936
01:29:09,123 --> 01:29:13,122
And what about Alex? You know, unfortunately,
we can't just keep him on ice.

937
01:29:13,600 --> 01:29:16,197
The shooting at the station
spooked some of the politicians.

938
01:29:16,197 --> 01:29:18,874
They're our clients.
We have to take care of them.

939
01:29:18,874 --> 01:29:22,391
They're fine when a machine
is lowering the murder rate, but,

940
01:29:22,391 --> 01:29:25,748
when a man is investigating
city politics, they get nervous.

941
01:29:25,748 --> 01:29:30,264
All right. First off, it's not a man,
okay? It's property of Omnicorp.

942
01:29:30,264 --> 01:29:34,421
And politics are the least of your concern.
I mean, this thing solved its own murder.

943
01:29:34,421 --> 01:29:36,899
How long till it realizes you
haven't been on the level with it?

944
01:29:36,899 --> 01:29:41,095
If that happens, every journalist in
this country is dying to speak to him.

945
01:29:41,095 --> 01:29:43,262
I mean, we created a hero.

946
01:29:43,614 --> 01:29:46,462
What happens when he opens his mouth?

947
01:29:49,768 --> 01:29:51,696
What's bigger than a hero?

948
01:30:03,157 --> 01:30:04,641
Dead hero.

949
01:30:08,752 --> 01:30:10,918
Get me Dr. Norton.

950
01:30:19,782 --> 01:30:21,107
What is this, Raymond?

951
01:30:22,020 --> 01:30:26,175
You have Mattox spying on me and now this
bullshit about a "critical condition"?

952
01:30:26,175 --> 01:30:32,050
You know and I know Alex is fine.
Calm down. Dennett.

953
01:30:32,050 --> 01:30:34,728
Your work is so good, I don't...
Well, now, this is not about my work.

954
01:30:34,728 --> 01:30:39,133
You saw the woman on TV.
This has to stop.

955
01:30:40,764 --> 01:30:42,248
You're right.

956
01:30:42,762 --> 01:30:44,919
But let me ask you something, Dennett.

957
01:30:44,919 --> 01:30:47,437
What kind of life have we
really given Alex Murphy?

958
01:30:47,437 --> 01:30:51,073
He's never going to be a normal
man, a father, a husband.

959
01:30:51,073 --> 01:30:55,751
By the time we put the other units
on the street, he's just... Dennett.

960
01:30:57,429 --> 01:30:59,152
Let's face it.

961
01:30:59,787 --> 01:31:01,475
We failed him.

962
01:31:02,744 --> 01:31:04,741
We failed Alex Murphy.

963
01:31:04,741 --> 01:31:08,059
But I want you to think about the bigger
picture because that's what we're talking about.

964
01:31:08,059 --> 01:31:10,896
The work you have done with him is
going to be studied for decades.

965
01:31:10,896 --> 01:31:13,174
You have changed the face
of history, Dennett.

966
01:31:13,174 --> 01:31:17,695
No policeman is ever going to
die in the line of duty again...

967
01:31:18,211 --> 01:31:19,979
...because of you.

968
01:31:21,448 --> 01:31:23,091
You think about that.

969
01:31:31,399 --> 01:31:36,993
I want that family taken care of
beyond their wildest dreams.

970
01:31:36,993 --> 01:31:39,274
- We owe them that.
- I agree.

971
01:31:39,832 --> 01:31:43,351
I want full funding. Ten years.

972
01:31:43,351 --> 01:31:47,155
New staff, all my own people.
Fantastic.

973
01:31:47,665 --> 01:31:48,865
Deal.

974
01:31:59,015 --> 01:32:02,571
Hey. What's going on? Security's here.
They're clearing everyone out.

975
01:32:02,571 --> 01:32:06,467
They're not waking him up.
Whatever you do, don't leave him alone.

976
01:32:06,467 --> 01:32:08,446
What do you mean they're
not waking him up?

977
01:32:09,885 --> 01:32:14,081
The voting period has ended.
The clerks have tabulated the results.

978
01:32:14,081 --> 01:32:16,199
The yeas are 63.

979
01:32:16,199 --> 01:32:21,554
The nays are 22. A majority of
senators have voted in the affirmative.

980
01:32:21,554 --> 01:32:25,391
The Dreyfus Act has been
repealed by Congress.

981
01:32:30,827 --> 01:32:34,622
God, you guys are slow,
like a bunch of girls. This is Mattox.

982
01:32:34,622 --> 01:32:37,865
Bennett's on board.
It's about time.

983
01:32:42,736 --> 01:32:44,061
Call it.

984
01:32:44,615 --> 01:32:46,224
Get it done.

985
01:32:47,053 --> 01:32:48,662
My pleasure.

986
01:32:57,164 --> 01:32:59,441
- Mrs. Murphy...
- You can come here as much as you want.

987
01:32:59,441 --> 01:33:02,798
You can threaten me. You can sue me.
You can take my home.

988
01:33:02,798 --> 01:33:05,920
But I am not going to stop till I see
my husband. Do you understand that?

989
01:33:05,920 --> 01:33:08,958
Mr. Sellars would very
much like to see you.

990
01:33:10,272 --> 01:33:15,586
Is Alex okay? He has important information
to share with you. Will you accompany me?

991
01:33:17,825 --> 01:33:19,185
David.

992
01:33:20,703 --> 01:33:23,020
We got to go.
Can you grab your coat?

993
01:33:24,300 --> 01:33:28,135
Hey. I am in the elevator,
on my way down. I need access to the lab.

994
01:33:28,135 --> 01:33:32,938
That's insane. They're still here.
Distract them. Okay.

995
01:33:33,971 --> 01:33:37,327
I cannot...
There's a lady in here going hysterical.

996
01:33:37,327 --> 01:33:39,286
She will not let us in.
She's got the codes for the door.

997
01:33:39,286 --> 01:33:41,044
I repeat, she will not let us in.

998
01:33:41,044 --> 01:33:43,402
Lady, you need to let us in there now.
We have to get in there.

999
01:33:43,402 --> 01:33:45,001
Are you not understanding
what I am saying?

1000
01:33:45,001 --> 01:33:49,597
Do you want to be responsible for the deaths
of everyone in this building? Hey. Stop.

1001
01:33:53,674 --> 01:33:56,437
Don't shoot.
Step outside.

1002
01:34:02,706 --> 01:34:04,588
Unlock the transmitter.

1003
01:34:05,743 --> 01:34:06,943
Transmitter unlocked.

1004
01:34:14,216 --> 01:34:18,093
Send in Mrs. Murphy, please.
Right away, sir.

1005
01:34:19,811 --> 01:34:21,250
Wake him up.

1006
01:34:21,250 --> 01:34:24,730
Alex. Alex.

1007
01:34:24,966 --> 01:34:29,608
Alex, it's Dr. Norton, you have to wake up.
Alex, can you hear me?

1008
01:34:30,961 --> 01:34:35,443
These men are here to kill us.
They're here to kill us, for chrissakes.

1009
01:34:40,113 --> 01:34:43,989
Mrs. Murphy, last night,
Alex had a psychotic break.

1010
01:34:43,989 --> 01:34:48,510
He killed an unarmed colleague
and later suffered a seizure.

1011
01:34:49,425 --> 01:34:54,145
We did everything, everything, we could,
but the doctors couldn't save him.

1012
01:34:55,380 --> 01:34:57,626
Very sorry, Mrs. Murphy.

1013
01:34:57,626 --> 01:35:00,466
We're going to be making
the announcement shortly.

1014
01:35:00,735 --> 01:35:03,379
You shut me down.
I was about to get a confession.

1015
01:35:03,812 --> 01:35:05,661
Mattox shut you down.

1016
01:35:06,810 --> 01:35:09,897
I have removed your transmitter
so he won't do it again.

1017
01:35:09,897 --> 01:35:12,447
Sellars can't afford to wake you up.

1018
01:35:13,284 --> 01:35:15,644
He sent these guys to pull the plug.

1019
01:35:15,882 --> 01:35:19,558
He wants you dead, Alex.
Do you understand?

1020
01:35:19,558 --> 01:35:22,955
Sorry. If there's anything we can
do for you and David, we will do it.

1021
01:35:22,955 --> 01:35:25,315
I want nothing from you.

1022
01:35:26,033 --> 01:35:27,562
I understand.

1023
01:35:27,911 --> 01:35:30,430
You stay out of our lives.

1024
01:35:31,628 --> 01:35:33,033
You and your company.

1025
01:35:33,033 --> 01:35:35,234
If that's what you think is best.

1026
01:35:35,984 --> 01:35:37,502
There's one more thing.

1027
01:35:37,502 --> 01:35:42,825
I think it would be to the benefit of everyone,
especially David if we kept this matter private.

1028
01:35:42,825 --> 01:35:45,622
We don't want to damage Alex's legacy.

1029
01:35:48,093 --> 01:35:50,135
Alex. Alex. Alex.

1030
01:35:50,135 --> 01:35:53,568
I can fix this.
You lied to me.

1031
01:35:53,568 --> 01:35:56,605
You lied to my wife. You're working for
the people that are trying to kill me.

1032
01:35:56,605 --> 01:36:00,171
You want me to trust you, Doctor?
Alex, I can go to the press.

1033
01:36:01,402 --> 01:36:04,170
Alex, I can tell them the whole story.

1034
01:36:04,170 --> 01:36:05,923
Alex.

1035
01:36:06,277 --> 01:36:08,399
Listen to me, please.

1036
01:36:09,195 --> 01:36:12,680
Alex. Alex.

1037
01:36:24,102 --> 01:36:25,348
What the hell?

1038
01:36:33,534 --> 01:36:37,129
Keep all our systems at green and for
chrissakes, get Sellars on the phone.

1039
01:36:37,129 --> 01:36:40,376
Roger that.
Damn, damn, damn, damn, damn.

1040
01:36:41,526 --> 01:36:43,295
Look at this city.

1041
01:36:44,924 --> 01:36:46,692
So beautiful.

1042
01:36:47,481 --> 01:36:50,364
It's become so peaceful.

1043
01:36:52,956 --> 01:36:54,486
I wish

1044
01:36:55,274 --> 01:36:57,713
I had some good news for Detroit.

1045
01:36:58,032 --> 01:36:59,949
I have very sad news.

1046
01:36:59,949 --> 01:37:05,551
Despite our best efforts to save him,
Alex Murphy passed away just hours ago.

1047
01:37:05,785 --> 01:37:08,623
Alex Murphy was... Mr. Sellars.

1048
01:37:08,623 --> 01:37:10,551
- What is it?
- Mattox just called.

1049
01:37:10,941 --> 01:37:12,982
We need you to come with us now.

1050
01:37:19,054 --> 01:37:20,971
Ma'am, I need you to turn around
and go the other way, please.

1051
01:37:20,971 --> 01:37:23,049
- What are you talking about?
- We have a security situation here.

1052
01:37:23,049 --> 01:37:24,568
I need you to turn around
and go the other way.

1053
01:37:24,568 --> 01:37:27,845
Sir, there's a car outside that's supposed
to... That area is locked down. Now go.

1054
01:37:27,845 --> 01:37:30,094
- What's happening?
- I said go.

1055
01:37:30,094 --> 01:37:32,444
I want to talk to Mr. Sellars.

1056
01:37:35,159 --> 01:37:38,797
Mr. Sellars. How close is that helicopter?
About 10 minutes, sir.

1057
01:37:56,181 --> 01:38:00,096
Excuse me. Yes? I need to speak with
Sergeant Jack Lewis.

1058
01:38:00,096 --> 01:38:03,299
It's an emergency.
Stand by. Mr. Sellars.

1059
01:38:03,574 --> 01:38:05,452
Apparently there's a Clara
Murphy in the lobby.

1060
01:38:05,452 --> 01:38:08,929
Raymond, if she sees him,
we are dead in the water.

1061
01:38:08,929 --> 01:38:12,846
- What do you want to do?
- Bring Mrs. Murphy up here. Yes, sir.

1062
01:38:16,443 --> 01:38:19,399
Norton said they may be using
drones for protection.

1063
01:38:19,399 --> 01:38:21,598
So whatever you do,
do not draw your weapons.

1064
01:38:21,598 --> 01:38:25,516
They won't shoot if we're unarmed.
Clear? Clear. Clear.

1065
01:38:41,701 --> 01:38:43,500
Hold it right there.

1066
01:38:44,059 --> 01:38:45,259
Don't move.

1067
01:38:47,915 --> 01:38:52,380
This is private property.
You are not authorized to be here.

1068
01:38:56,088 --> 01:39:00,563
I'd put those guns down now if I were you.
Stand down. All right, man, we're good.

1069
01:39:03,161 --> 01:39:04,345
Back it up.

1070
01:39:46,684 --> 01:39:48,213
Head to the lower level.

1071
01:39:49,641 --> 01:39:52,165
- Hold up, hold up.
- Ram it.

1072
01:40:52,186 --> 01:40:53,671
Gun it.

1073
01:40:54,644 --> 01:40:56,712
Go. Go, go. Now.

1074
01:41:12,488 --> 01:41:14,177
Alex, run.

1075
01:41:14,806 --> 01:41:19,082
Omnicorp Security.
Drop your weapons. Drop your weapon.

1076
01:41:19,082 --> 01:41:22,090
Keep your hands above your head
and no one will be harmed.

1077
01:41:37,147 --> 01:41:40,783
What's going on? Mrs. Murphy,
I want you to listen to me carefully.

1078
01:41:40,783 --> 01:41:43,340
The organic part of your
husband Alex is dead.

1079
01:41:43,340 --> 01:41:46,737
The robotic part of him is malfunctioning,
and he's shooting up the building.

1080
01:41:46,737 --> 01:41:49,695
So we have got to get you and your
son out of here right away.

1081
01:41:49,695 --> 01:41:51,419
I got to take this call.

1082
01:41:52,533 --> 01:41:55,940
He just left the lobby and he's headed
our way. Roger that, sir.

1083
01:41:55,940 --> 01:42:00,806
- Don't shoot. My robot. You just flank.
- Got it. Tin Man.

1084
01:42:03,364 --> 01:42:04,768
Tin Man.

1085
01:42:05,602 --> 01:42:07,040
Tin Man.

1086
01:42:07,040 --> 01:42:08,800
Oh, there it is.

1087
01:42:09,278 --> 01:42:10,842
You look like crap.

1088
01:42:13,275 --> 01:42:15,999
What's the matter?
Can't shoot?

1089
01:42:17,591 --> 01:42:18,871
Huh?

1090
01:42:19,430 --> 01:42:22,788
What were you thinking?
This isn't a drill. You're a robot.

1091
01:42:22,788 --> 01:42:25,231
I am a red asset. Wrote that myself.

1092
01:42:25,464 --> 01:42:26,994
What do you think?

1093
01:42:26,994 --> 01:42:31,380
Come on, Tin Man, just pull the trigger.
Pull it.

1094
01:42:31,979 --> 01:42:33,258
You can run.

1095
01:42:33,617 --> 01:42:34,817
Go on.

1096
01:42:34,817 --> 01:42:36,181
Run.

1097
01:42:36,455 --> 01:42:37,779
Run.

1098
01:42:37,779 --> 01:42:39,935
There you go. Run.

1099
01:42:40,171 --> 01:42:41,735
Run. Run.

1100
01:42:44,687 --> 01:42:48,483
Whoo.
Stings like a bitch, don't it?

1101
01:42:48,483 --> 01:42:51,840
Aren't you lucky I didn't
have my gun set to "kill"?

1102
01:42:53,040 --> 01:42:54,570
Hey, listen.

1103
01:42:54,798 --> 01:42:56,601
This isn't personal.

1104
01:42:57,436 --> 01:42:59,398
Well, maybe a little.

1105
01:43:00,953 --> 01:43:02,950
I am going to put you
out of your misery.

1106
01:43:14,501 --> 01:43:17,378
Helicopter's approaching.
Mr. Sellars boards first.

1107
01:43:17,378 --> 01:43:20,546
No, no, no. Mrs. Murphy, you
and your son can get on first.

1108
01:43:25,731 --> 01:43:28,328
Officer down.
Mechanical room.

1109
01:43:28,328 --> 01:43:32,166
Omnicorp Building.
Roger that. EMS on the way.

1110
01:43:33,564 --> 01:43:38,364
You're going to be okay, Jack.
It's nonfatal. Go. Go.

1111
01:43:39,359 --> 01:43:42,367
Omni-LZ Helo-1 on approach to deck.

1112
01:43:48,911 --> 01:43:50,111
What's that?

1113
01:43:51,828 --> 01:43:54,307
- He's got a gun.
- What? Pull up. Pull up.

1114
01:43:59,062 --> 01:44:01,581
- What the hell is he doing?
- Sorry, sir. I don't know.

1115
01:44:06,895 --> 01:44:09,300
Alex?
Dad?

1116
01:44:12,490 --> 01:44:14,100
Clara, David.

1117
01:44:14,888 --> 01:44:17,367
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa. Wait.

1118
01:44:18,245 --> 01:44:20,282
- Get out of the way.
- Alex, put down the gun.

1119
01:44:20,282 --> 01:44:22,563
Clara, take David and
get out of the way now.

1120
01:44:24,240 --> 01:44:27,677
Raymond Sellars, you're under arrest
for the attempted murder of a police officer.

1121
01:44:31,154 --> 01:44:33,877
Are you here to cuff me? All right.

1122
01:44:34,471 --> 01:44:39,785
Go ahead, cuff me. You can't.
You're not programmed that way.

1123
01:44:39,785 --> 01:44:43,382
If you go against the program,
the entire system shuts down, so.

1124
01:44:43,382 --> 01:44:45,620
You don't even have a warrant.
We will overlook this little...

1125
01:44:45,620 --> 01:44:47,858
Get down on the ground and put
your hands behind your back.

1126
01:44:47,858 --> 01:44:51,535
I am just from marketing.
Now. Okay, yep, yep, yep. Yep.

1127
01:44:51,535 --> 01:44:53,853
Alex, we need to work together here.

1128
01:44:53,853 --> 01:44:57,180
Because I am the only one with the
technology to keep you alive.

1129
01:44:58,090 --> 01:44:59,893
Dead or alive, you're coming with me.

1130
01:45:05,843 --> 01:45:08,202
All right.
Weapon.

1131
01:45:09,680 --> 01:45:12,956
Alex, honestly, I mean you no harm.

1132
01:45:12,956 --> 01:45:15,434
If I wanted to, I could have
killed you a long time ago.

1133
01:45:15,434 --> 01:45:19,390
I just aim this right at your head and
blow it off. Sellars, please. Don't.

1134
01:45:19,390 --> 01:45:22,230
I mean, if I wanted to, I could
just aim this at your little family

1135
01:45:23,268 --> 01:45:24,946
and I could just kill them too.

1136
01:45:24,946 --> 01:45:28,905
And really, there's nothing you could
do about it because, let's face it,

1137
01:45:29,343 --> 01:45:30,872
you're a robot.

1138
01:45:31,301 --> 01:45:32,945
Do you understand that?

1139
01:45:37,016 --> 01:45:38,216
Alex.

1140
01:45:41,172 --> 01:45:42,611
Dad.

1141
01:45:46,528 --> 01:45:48,012
Baby.

1142
01:45:53,362 --> 01:45:54,686
Hey.

1143
01:45:56,079 --> 01:45:57,279
Hey.

1144
01:45:57,598 --> 01:45:59,798
Everything's going to be all right.

1145
01:46:00,555 --> 01:46:02,994
Everything's going to be all right.

1146
01:46:52,629 --> 01:46:54,592
How you feeling, Alex?

1147
01:46:56,306 --> 01:46:57,631
I am ready.

1148
01:47:35,192 --> 01:47:36,756
He's ready.

1149
01:48:10,641 --> 01:48:15,081
There's still no word from
Omnicorp parent company, OCP.

1150
01:48:15,796 --> 01:48:19,632
And although the government says
they are rebuilding Alex Murphy,

1151
01:48:19,632 --> 01:48:22,430
rumors continue to swirl
about his condition.

1152
01:48:22,430 --> 01:48:27,065
But we have obtained exclusive
video taken by cell phone

1153
01:48:27,065 --> 01:48:31,741
that shows the people of Detroit may
have Alex Murphy back on the streets

1154
01:48:31,741 --> 01:48:33,511
sooner than they think.

1155
01:48:35,339 --> 01:48:41,934
The real tragedy here is that our
president chose to uphold the Dreyfus Act.

1156
01:48:43,092 --> 01:48:47,627
Now, I have no doubt he was
manipulated by our biased media

1157
01:48:47,627 --> 01:48:51,484
and by whistle-blower Dennett Norton.

1158
01:48:51,484 --> 01:48:55,448
I acknowledge we know
less than we thought.

1159
01:48:56,241 --> 01:48:59,362
But I do believe my
research program is sound.

1160
01:49:00,717 --> 01:49:02,202
What I did with it

1161
01:49:03,475 --> 01:49:04,593
was wrong.

1162
01:49:04,593 --> 01:49:07,710
The fact that this mother...

1163
01:49:07,710 --> 01:49:15,229
is not serving time in some federal penitentiary
is a huge, hot, heaping pile of horse...

1164
01:49:20,779 --> 01:49:25,254
Now I know some of you may think that
this kind of thinking is dangerous

1165
01:49:25,254 --> 01:49:29,411
and these machines violate
your civil liberties.

1166
01:49:29,411 --> 01:49:33,607
Some of you even believe that the
use of these drones overseas

1167
01:49:33,607 --> 01:49:38,363
makes us the same kind
of bullying imperialists

1168
01:49:38,363 --> 01:49:41,326
that our forefathers
were trying to escape.

1169
01:49:41,561 --> 01:49:44,198
To you, I say...

1170
01:49:44,198 --> 01:49:46,763
Stop whining.

1171
